---
// src/pages/projects/spatial-map.astro
import "../../styles/global.css";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" class="scroll-smooth">
	<head>
		<meta charset="UTF-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
		<title>Gerard Baldo | Spatial Map Case Study</title>
		<script is:inline>
			(function() {
				const savedTheme = localStorage.getItem('theme');
				if (savedTheme === 'light') {
					document.documentElement.classList.add('light');
				} else {
					document.documentElement.classList.remove('light');
				}
			})();
		</script>
	</head>
	<body
		class="bg-neutral-950 text-neutral-100 font-sans selection:bg-neutral-800 antialiased"
	>
		<div class="flex min-h-screen">
			<aside
				class="fixed top-0 left-0 h-screen w-64 border-r border-neutral-800 bg-neutral-950 p-6 flex flex-col justify-between z-50"
			>
				<div class="flex flex-col gap-8">
					<div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
						<div
							class="h-14 w-14 rounded-lg bg-neutral-900 border border-neutral-800 flex items-center justify-center text-lg font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-300"
						>
							GB
						</div>
						<div>
							<h2
								class="font-semibold text-neutral-200 tracking-tight"
							>
								Gerard Baldo
							</h2>
							<p class="text-xs text-neutral-500 font-mono">
								System-First Engineer
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<nav class="flex flex-col gap-2 text-sm">
						<a
							href="/"
							class="text-neutral-400 hover:text-neutral-100 transition-colors py-1.5 font-medium font-mono text-xs tracking-wider"
							>➔ RETURN_HOME</a
						>
					</nav>
				</div>

				<div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
					<button
						id="theme-toggle"
						class="flex items-center justify-between w-full border border-neutral-800 hover:border-neutral-700 bg-neutral-900/10 hover:bg-neutral-900/30 text-neutral-400 hover:text-neutral-200 transition-all rounded px-3 py-2 text-xs font-mono select-none cursor-pointer"
					>
						<span>THEME: DEFAULT (DARK)</span>
						<span id="theme-icon">☼</span>
					</button>

					<div
						class="text-[10px] text-neutral-500 font-mono flex items-center gap-2 tracking-tight"
					>
						<span
							class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-500 animate-pulse"
						></span>
						<span>ENVIRONMENT: ACTIVE</span>
					</div>
				</div>
			</aside>

			<main
				class="ml-64 flex-1 px-8 md:px-16 py-16 max-w-4xl flex flex-col gap-8"
			>
				<a href="/" class="text-xs font-mono text-neutral-500 hover:text-neutral-300 transition-colors self-start">
					// BACK_TO_DASHBOARD
				</a>

				<section class="border border-neutral-800 bg-neutral-900/30 rounded-xl p-8 backdrop-blur-sm">
					<span class="text-[10px] font-mono text-neutral-500 uppercase tracking-widest">// Case Study</span>
					<h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mt-2 mb-4 tracking-tight text-neutral-100">
						Unified Intake & Spatial Mapping Engine
					</h1>
					<p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed text-sm md:text-base">
						A complete restructuring of a legacy government profiling form into a dynamic relational intake system featuring zero-friction GIS coordinate mapping.
					</p>

					<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mt-6">
						<span class="px-2 py-1 text-xs font-mono rounded bg-neutral-900 text-neutral-400 border border-neutral-800">Leaflet.js</span>
						<span class="px-2 py-1 text-xs font-mono rounded bg-neutral-900 text-neutral-400 border border-neutral-800">Dynamic DOM Repeater</span>
						<span class="px-2 py-1 text-xs font-mono rounded bg-neutral-900 text-neutral-400 border border-neutral-800">Vanilla JS State</span>
						<span class="px-2 py-1 text-xs font-mono rounded bg-neutral-900 text-neutral-400 border border-neutral-800">DSWD Pag Abot</span>
					</div>
				</section>

				<section class="border border-neutral-800 bg-neutral-900/10 rounded-xl p-8 flex flex-col gap-6">
					<div>
						<h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-neutral-200 mb-3 tracking-tight">// THE BOTTLENECK & THE TASK</h2>
						<p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
							The Pag Abot Program targets individuals and families in street situations (FISS), providing critical social rescue and long-term reintegration. When field operations deployed, operators faced massive frictional gridlock caused by their core data-collection tool: <strong>the legacy intake form was rigid and address-dependent.</strong>
						</p>
						<p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
							Because beneficiaries are frequently located under overpasses, on street corners, or near landmarks with zero structured physical addresses, traditional text logging broke. Furthermore, processing entire family structures was highly inefficient—the old interface could not scale fluidly to account for multiple family members encountered together on-site.
						</p>
						<p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
							Prior development teams stalled trying to implement coordinate tracking and dynamic layouts. My supervisors handed me the task from scratch: refactor the entire collection component to introduce seamless, high-velocity profiling and multi-member data integrity within a unified workspace.
						</p>
					</div>

					<hr class="border-neutral-800/80" />

					<div>
						<h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-neutral-200 mb-3 tracking-tight">// INTENTIONALLY ENGINEERED ARCHITECTURE</h2>
						
						<h3 class="text-xs font-mono text-neutral-300 uppercase tracking-wider mb-2 mt-4">1. Relational Intake Form & Dynamic Sub-Form Repeater</h3>
						<p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
							To maximize field intake speed, I re-engineered the legacy fill-up form into a responsive, clean DOM controller. I integrated a specific classification toggle that allowed operators to instantly flag an individual's location context (e.g., street-level environment vs. structured shelter).
						</p>
						<p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
							To map families cohabiting in these environments, I engineered a **dynamic nested sub-form repeater**. Instead of routing operators through complex secondary pages, a single button click instantly instantiates and injects a clean, secondary family intake container directly into the active view. Each sub-form automatically tracks relational data—binding the family member directly to the primary beneficiary node while maintaining field validation arrays on the client side.
						</p>

						<h3 class="text-xs font-mono text-neutral-300 uppercase tracking-wider mb-2 mt-4">2. Zero-Friction GIS Isolation: Leaflet over Google</h3>
						<p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-wider mb-4">
							When adding the cartographic tracking layer, the mainstream solution was Google Maps API. However, this presented organizational friction: it required billing profiles, API key bindings, and permanent account setups. Because I was developing this as an intern, tying critical infrastructure to temporary profiles risked severe deployment issues later.
						</p>
						<p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
							Prioritizing a **seamless, frictionless corporate handoff**, I integrated <strong>Leaflet.js</strong>. It was light, fast, customizable, and ran entirely token-free, allowing the team to adopt the code base instantly with absolute zero authentication management or billing configuration overhead.
						</p>

						<h3 class="text-xs font-mono text-neutral-300 uppercase tracking-wider mb-2 mt-4">3. Reclaiming Dormant Database Schemas</h3>
						<p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
							Completed in a rapid 3-to-4 day development cycle, my prototype was wired straight into the application's underlying submission pipeline. During my analysis of the core application layout, I discovered that the existing database schema and system API already possessed unmapped, dormant spatial coordinate columns that were sitting completely unused. 
						</p>
						<p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
							I calibrated the dynamic form's payload format to feed latitude/longitude data directly into those exact waiting structures, passing data safely through the pre-configured backend API guardrails without needing any server-side database refactoring.
						</p>

						<h3 class="text-xs font-mono text-neutral-300 uppercase tracking-wider mb-2 mt-4">4. Defeating the Leaflet Container Trap</h3>
						<p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
							Embedding this new layout inside our clean, accordion-style project dashboard introduced a layout failure: initializing a Leaflet instance inside a hidden element (`display: none`) strips its capability to calculate real layout widths. When expanded, the map would render corrupted tiles and shattered boundaries.
						</p>
						<p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
							I resolved this defensively by listening exclusively to the container card's `'toggle'` event. The GIS layer only initializes when physical heights are accurately computed in the DOM:
						</p>

						<div class="bg-neutral-950 border border-neutral-800 rounded-lg p-4 font-mono text-xs text-neutral-300 overflow-x-auto leading-relaxed mb-6">
							<span class="text-neutral-500">// Initialize GIS layer only when accordion actively opens to preserve layout heights</span><br />
							card.addEventListener(<span class="text-emerald-400">'toggle'</span>, () =&gt; &#123;<br />
							&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="text-amber-400">if</span> (card.open && !mapInitialized) &#123;<br />
							&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;initializeMapEngine();<br />
							&nbsp;&nbsp;&#125;<br />
							&#125;);
						</div>
					</div>
				</section>

				<section class="border border-neutral-800 bg-neutral-900/10 rounded-xl p-8 flex flex-col gap-6">
					<h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-neutral-200 tracking-tight">// SYSTEM DATA FLOW</h2>
					
					<div class="bg-neutral-950 border border-neutral-800 rounded-lg p-6 font-mono text-xs text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed overflow-x-auto">
<pre class="leading-normal">
 [Unified Intake Controller] ───► [Street Classification Toggle: ACTIVE]
              │
              ├─► [Add Family Member] ──► [Inject Dynamic Relational Form Node]
              │
              ▼
[Leaflet Map Canvas Mount]
              │
    ┌─────────┴─────────┐
    ▼                   ▼
[User Map Pin Click] [Manual Input Vector]
    │                   │
    ▼                   ▼
[Coordinate Capture] ──► [Input Synced & Validated]
                        │
                        ▼
             [Staged Payload Assembly]
             (Populating Dormant Spatial DB Columns)
</pre>
					</div>
				</section>
			</main>
		</div>

		<script is:inline>
			window.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
				// Theme Toggle Logic
				const themeToggleBtn = document.getElementById('theme-toggle');
				const themeIcon = document.getElementById('theme-icon');
				const themeText = themeToggleBtn.querySelector('span');

				function updateThemeUI(isLight) {
					if (isLight) {
						document.documentElement.classList.add('light');
						if (themeText) themeText.textContent = 'THEME: BEIGE_MODE';
						if (themeIcon) themeIcon.textContent = '☾';
					} else {
						document.documentElement.classList.remove('light');
						if (themeText) themeText.textContent = 'THEME: DEFAULT (DARK)';
						if (themeIcon) themeIcon.textContent = '☼';
					}
				}

				// Initialize UI state
				const isCurrentlyLight = document.documentElement.classList.contains('light');
				updateThemeUI(isCurrentlyLight);

				themeToggleBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
					const isLight = document.documentElement.classList.toggle('light');
					localStorage.setItem('theme', isLight ? 'light' : 'dark');
					updateThemeUI(isLight);
				});
			});
		</script>
	</body>
</html>
